WEBVTT

00:00:06.633 --> 00:00:12.366
Hey guys! We're studying different kinds of animals in science class.

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:16.800
Our class visited a wildlife centre last week.

00:00:18.233 --> 00:00:20.866
There were many animals at the centre.

00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:24.233
We didn't see any elephants,

00:00:24.233 --> 00:00:28.166
but we saw a mother bear and two baby bears.

00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:31.566
The mother bear was huge!

00:00:31.566 --> 00:00:34.699
She was the same size as a small car.

00:00:35.700 --> 00:00:38.700
I took this picture before they ran away.

00:00:39.133 --> 00:00:40.733
We saw a grey parrot.

00:00:41.466 --> 00:00:45.399
My friend Lily said, 'What a beautiful parrot!'

00:00:45.400 --> 00:00:49.400
And the parrot said, 'What a beautiful parrot!'

00:00:49.400 --> 00:00:53.866
Everyone laughed. Parrots are so clever!

00:00:55.233 --> 00:00:58.466
We saw a bunch of other animals, too.

00:00:58.633 --> 00:01:00.966
Like <i>this</i> long snake.

00:01:01.833 --> 00:01:04.833
The wildlife guide let us touch it.

00:01:04.833 --> 00:01:09.433
Ew! I didn't touch it, but my friend Ben did.

00:01:10.833 --> 00:01:16.499
It was an amazing trip! That's all. Bye!

00:01:22.566 --> 00:01:24.999
Which language does the vlogger use?

00:01:29.800 --> 00:01:34.200
We use the past simple to talk about actions that happened in the past.

00:01:37.066 --> 00:01:41.432
To form the past simple of regular verbs, we add – <i>ed</i> .</p>

00:01:42.966 --> 00:01:44.666
Everyone laughed.

00:01:46.200 --> 00:01:49.366
To form the past simple of irregular verbs,

00:01:49.366 --> 00:01:55.832
we use different words such as, <i>take/took</i> and <i>run/ran</i> .

00:01:57.300 --> 00:01:59.966
I took this picture before they ran away.

00:02:03.066 --> 00:02:05.332
To form the negative past simple,

00:02:05.333 --> 00:02:09.866
we use <i>did not</i> plus the infinitive without <i>to</i>.

00:02:10.766 --> 00:02:11.899
I didn't touch it.

00:02:13.033 --> 00:02:15.166
We didn't see any elephants.

00:02:20.133 --> 00:02:23.799
We often use past time expressions with the past simple.

00:02:24.733 --> 00:02:28.599
Our class visited a wildlife centre last week.

00:02:31.100 --> 00:02:33.500
<i>They didn't go to the centre yesterday.</i>

00:02:37.866 --> 00:02:38.499
<b>Use it!</b>

00:02:40.400 --> 00:02:41.300
What happened?

00:02:42.333 --> 00:02:44.733
Change the sentences to past tense.

00:02:57.433 --> 00:02:59.566
<i>The lion <b>ran</b> this morning.</i>

00:03:01.800 --> 00:03:02.666
Now you try.

00:03:12.366 --> 00:03:15.332
<i>The monkey <b>ate</b> a banana yesterday.</i>

00:03:28.066 --> 00:03:30.532
<i>We <b>saw</b> a koala sleeping yesterday.</i>

00:03:43.200 --> 00:03:46.133
<i>The whales <b>didn't swim</b> by the boat last month.</i>